WEBVTT

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:09.610
The second half of the fateful semifinals between Inazuma Japan and Mach Tiger is ready to begin!

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:12.500
What's the matter?

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.590
I'm a little worried about our fight for the second half.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.330
You too, huh?

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.900
Yeah. It's just a feeling, but...

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:26.710
Even though, by adding Morimura-san's defense into our calculations, we have the advantage...

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.540
Manabe. Minaho.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.170
You two must find it together.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.140
The answer key to victory.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.080
The answer key...

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.880
To victory...?

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:25.930
Here we are at the Asia district preliminary semifinals for FFI Vision 2!

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:29.880
The game is between Japan's Inazuma Japan and Thailand's Mach Tiger!

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.820
The score is currently at a 1-1 tie!

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:36.970
Who will advance to the finals, Inazuma Japan or Mach Tiger?

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:39.930
The second half is now starting!

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:43.300
The answer key to victory, huh?

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:47.850
<i>You two must find it together.</i>

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:51.690
I don't dislike the challenge of a difficult problem.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.110
I'll find it, before you do.

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:57.620
I wouldn't have it any other way.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.820
Don't back down from the other team, everyone!

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.310
Keep those spirits high!

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:05.580
Let's win this match, no matter what!

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:06.410
Yeah!

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:10.410
It's about time we showed them how much we should be feared.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:12.250
We will be the victors!

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:13.290
Yeah!

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.670
The second half starts!

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:19.950
What?!

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:23.340
Bark cuts for the ball and continues with dribbling!

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:25.260
They're focusing on offense for the second half, huh!

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:26.350
I won't let you!

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.510
What a tricky play!

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.480
Mach Tiger moves up boldly!

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:34.310
Tamugan!

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:39.190
Which side will Tamugan pass to?

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:42.360
Kaolan!

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.660
Oh dear, Minaho and Manabe were unable to make a move!

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.870
Leaf Roll!

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.960
Konoha, nice cut!

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:01.620
Hey!

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:05.300
C'mon guys, just standing there and watching is out of the question.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:07.750
We weren't just watching them.

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.270
Yes. Analyzing the opponent comes first and foremost.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.230
Besides, we have Morimura-san behind us.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:20.350
Now that we have her hissatsu technique on our side, our likelihood of stopping the opponent has soared.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:21.860
O-Oh, yeah?

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.240
T-Thanks.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:26.200
Tsurugi!

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.440
Is this a chance for Inazuma Japan?

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:30.410
We'll stop you!

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.660
Death Scythe Middle!

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:37.920
Sarit!

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:39.250
Tamugan!

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.680
Now, who will he pass to this time?!

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:49.130
What's important is which foot he puts his balance on before making the pass.

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:52.150
That analysis has too many inconclusive elements.

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.530
Judging from the angle of the two coming in to receive it...

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.100
Go to the right!

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:57.520
Bark!

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:02.110
Good job, Tetsukado!

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.290
Barely made it.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:09.780
If you weren't making side comments, we would have reached a faster conclusion.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:12.120
That's what I should be saying to you.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.000
Kaolan!

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.170
Nice cut, Shindou-san!

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:24.550
We're attacking without delay!

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:28.340
God's Baton: Fire Illusion!

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.100
Nozaki!

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.100
Okay!

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.100
I'll stop you!

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.850
Will Inazuma Japan make their counter?!

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:40.040
Hayato-niichan would have been able to do it.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.520
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:43.900
Nawat!

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:50.410
Tamugan!

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:55.080
Let's show them our true worth!

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:03.000
I can't determine his course from his pivot leg when he's up that high.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.690
The angle at which they're running in, speed, and timing of their jumps are exactly the same.

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:09.970
I'm not able to calculate their tendencies from here...

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:12.680
Bark!

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:14.520
Mei!

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:16.730
It's a fake.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:25.030
The ball turned...

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.660
Who is he going to pass to?

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:34.700
There's no way to calculate it.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.620
Your goal is wide-open!

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:39.710
Tamugan!

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.800
Ivory Crush!

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:53.510
Wild Dun-

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:55.560
It's fast!

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:58.310
Goal!

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:00.200
Mach Tiger takes their second point!

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:04.270
Tamugan makes in a magnificent shoot through tricky passwork!

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:06.510
No, it went in.

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:07.610
That can't be...

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:11.530
I can't block them all...

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:22.040
What was with that attack?

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.750
I couldn't tell how the ball would move at all.

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:26.250
Guys!

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.510
Don't give up yet!

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:29.670
Let's refocus ourselves!

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.130
We can get back a second point easily!

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.680
Don't feel rushed!

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:37.350
I'll make a more complete analysis next time.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:41.100
Once I capture their tendencies, I'll have a strategy against them!

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:46.650
Is it really a good idea to leave the outcome of this match to those two?

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:50.350
You getting upset won't change anything.

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:51.110
Am I wrong?

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:58.910
Isn't that your mother and father?

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:04.200
Papa, Mama!

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:05.540
Why?

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:12.950
Never mind that, finding the key to victory comes first.

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:13.880
Let's focus.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:15.680
You're right.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:25.150
How can I attack the opponent when they're able to make crazy moves like that?

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:26.650
Matatagi.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:29.860
A forward mustn't show irritation or worry.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.420
Keep your composure.

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:33.820
But...

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:34.660
Matatagi.

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:39.110
Let's bring the ball up little by little, passing before the opponent marks us.

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:41.310
I'm sure a chance will come!

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:42.250
Okay!

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:45.250
That's good, Tenma.

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:48.380
Now, the match resumes!

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:50.050
Captain!

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:50.710
An opening!

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:53.720
Tamugan!

00:08:56.710 --> 00:09:00.150
There has to be something where I can make a distinction...

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:01.680
Who is he going to pass to?

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:05.690
Is it the acceleration of their jump... no, the angle at their jump's timing?

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:06.840
Right side!

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:09.860
No way!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.130
I can't believe your prediction was wrong.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:21.200
Papa...

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.950
This method is too exhaustive.

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:28.420
If you'd used graphs, you could have reduced your time by five minutes.

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:32.000
Just finding the correct answer isn't enough.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.970
You must reach the solution efficiently.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:41.910
Good grief... if a problem of this level is giving you trouble, you're going to have a hard life ahead of you.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:43.930
I'm sorry...

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:48.730
Manabe?

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:57.200
The number of rotations in the ball... it's the same pattern as before!

00:09:57.800 --> 00:09:59.570
The ball is going to curve right!

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:05.040
The other way? That can't be!

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:11.500
Kusaka-kun...

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:18.090
Is there something wrong, Manabe-kun?

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.720
If you hadn't told me what I didn't need to hear...!

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:23.420
Manabe-kun?

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:31.730
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:36.660
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:47.310
Papa...

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:48.330
Manabe-kun?

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.290
Could it be that you and your father...?

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:53.290
That's none of your business!

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:58.300
Go right!

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:07.310
At that velocity, I can dodge him!

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:13.150
Right! N-No, I mean, left!

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:16.190
Oh no!

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:21.910
My calculations should have been perfect...

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:22.930
Manabe-kun.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:26.410
Remember what you said to me last time?

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:32.420
<i>Parents only think about pushing their values on their children and trying to control them.</i>

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:40.710
After remembering your words and watching how you behaved once you knew your parents were in the stands, I understood.

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:42.270
You want your parents...

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:46.310
Or more specifically, you want your father to acknowledge you.

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:47.760
I think that's how you feel.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:51.480
I wish you wouldn't speak on assumption, without any facts to back you up.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:54.550
It's not your father whom you hate.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:58.440
You hate yourself for being unable to meet your father's expectations.

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:09.950
Tsurugi!

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:12.470
Are you okay?

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:13.330
Yeah...

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:14.240
Bark...

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:16.910
That's not true!

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:20.300
Stop talking nonsense!

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.160
What's up with those two?

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:23.050
No idea...

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:28.510
But I don't understand why you're trying to avoid your father...

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:33.020
I'm sure you wouldn't. Not when you're on such good terms with your father even now!

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.230
Minaho! Manabe!

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:38.620
What are you doing?

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:39.940
We're in the middle of a game!

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:42.860
No, let me say a few words on this.

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:46.670
I understand that you have a really good relationship with your father.

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:50.410
But that gives no right for you to make comments about me and Papa!

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:56.040
I bet your father understands you and praises you, does he?

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:58.820
Then why not just leave it at that?

00:12:59.180 --> 00:13:02.950
Even if I wanted my dad to look at me, he can't do that anymore.

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:07.260
He passed away a long time ago.

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:09.640
Passed away?

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:12.140
When I was younger.

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:14.260
Minaho...

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:16.400
I'm envious of you.

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:22.110
For as long as I can remember, I've always wanted to become someone like my dad.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:24.110
That's so cool, Dad!

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:28.200
Yes. I didn't expect to receive the Commissioner's Award.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.910
It's the greatest honor to be given among the police forces.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:34.120
As expected from the famous detective who can solve any case.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:36.620
Dad's a hero of justice!

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:39.820
Yeah! Justice will prevail!

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:40.840
Did I sound the part?

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:47.600
It's the medal for the Commissioner's Award.

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:50.620
I'm gonna be a detective just like you!

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:53.770
I'll solve all kinds of cases like you do!

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:55.450
Yeah!

00:13:55.450 --> 00:14:01.370
Even if I want to follow my dad's example and do better than him, he's no longer here to act as my role model.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:06.310
I don't have someone to follow in their footsteps anymore.

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:08.240
Minaho-kun...

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:10.310
But not you.

00:14:10.310 --> 00:14:14.310
Having a father around will help you to grow immensely.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:17.210
I know that better than anyone.

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:25.690
But even when I'm thinking clearly, I find it hard to believe that I'll be able to grow in this match...

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:28.220
Maybe even finding the key to victory is impossible...

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:30.290
Manabe-kun...

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:32.480
Do you really think that?

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:36.870
If you don't, then I don't want you to give up.

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:42.520
Besides, I believe that with your skills, you two will be able to find the key to victory!

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:44.520
Captain.

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:50.070
The match resumes with Tetsukado's throw-in!

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.070
Sakura!

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:55.470
Tamugan steals the ball!

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:57.950
Without even a breath of pause, Mach Tiger attacks!

00:14:57.950 --> 00:15:00.540
Inazuma Japan is forced into a tough fight!

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:04.260
Manabe-kun.

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:07.840
Your father's been watching only you this whole time.

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:15.000
Whenever you face a dangerous play, he pulls at the knot of his necktie.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.100
It's proof that he's worried about you.

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:21.060
It looks to me that your father doesn't hate you at all.

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:23.400
Papa...

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:25.270
Sarit!

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.280
I'll stop you here!

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:30.650
Again!

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:33.870
Papa is watching me.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:40.530
I'll find the answer to victory!

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:44.250
<i>You must reach the solution efficiently!</i>

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:45.620
Minaho-kun!

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:52.010
Complementing your predictions with mine may be the shortcut to reaching the answer key to victory.

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:54.710
Complementing?

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:56.720
That sounds interesting.

00:15:57.110 --> 00:16:00.730
So, in other words, I base my predictions on observation and behavioral analysis...

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:04.890
And I will handle analyzing the mathematical data.

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:07.450
Don't think badly of us.

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:09.690
The third point is ours!

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:13.150
I found it.

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:17.650
His arm that's opposite of the direction he's passing to raises up a little.

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:18.160
In other words...

00:16:18.690 --> 00:16:19.410
It's the left!

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:20.160
What?!

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:21.500
Sarana!

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:25.000
The number of rotations of the ball, its speed, the direction of the wind...

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:27.000
It's going left!

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:38.550
From that dribbling speed, the position and angle from which I can steal the ball is 3*-4+β...

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:39.890
I see it!

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:46.730
Defense Equation!

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:52.110
Wow...

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:53.320
You did it, Manabe!

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:54.530
I'll stop you!

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:58.280
Manabe-kun, I'll get it back!

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:01.120
Trace Press!

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.330
What?

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:08.480
Minaho just...!

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:09.500
Him, too?

00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:12.460
Those two succeeded.

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:14.220
W-Wow!

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:18.000
Is this the result of their synergy?

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.680
They finally found the answer.

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:22.680
Matatagi-kun!

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:25.440
Go, Nii-chan!

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:29.270
You're not going anywhere!

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:31.780
Go for it!

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:32.900
I'll make it in!

00:17:33.930 --> 00:17:36.030
Bicycle Sword!

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:41.910
Goal!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:45.460
Tsurugi's shoot brings Inazuma Japan up to a tie!

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:47.220
The clock is ticking!

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:49.880
Which team will rise to the top?!

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:52.880
Losing for us is not an option!

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:02.640
Ivory Crush!

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:05.560
I'll stop you!

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.440
Wild Dunk!

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.110
Nice save, Ibuki!

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:16.570
I stopped it this time!

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:23.970
Don't let your guard down, everyone!

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:26.120
It's just one more point! Let's go get it!

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:29.620
Tetsukado!

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:37.380
The weight he puts on his pivot leg...

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:38.910
Go left! It'll work!

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:40.130
Right!

00:18:40.130 --> 00:18:40.680
Morimura!

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:44.690
Pass to Kusaka-kun!

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:46.430
You'll have a 92% rate of success!

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:47.680
Okay!

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:52.150
They're going in for a sliding!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:55.480
Nozaki!

00:18:58.130 --> 00:18:59.990
Nozaki-san, you'll beat them with your leg strength!

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:04.370
Matatagi!

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:07.450
That facial expression...

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:08.330
They're ready to charge you!

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:10.080
Shindou-san!

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:14.340
You won't make it! Back pass!

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:15.920
Tsurugi!

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:20.750
Those movements... They're about to use a hissatsu technique!

00:19:22.310 --> 00:19:23.680
Tenma, go for it!

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:26.930
Please!

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:27.720
I'll make it in!

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.560
God Wind!

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:38.990
Killer Elbow!

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:45.870
Goal!

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:46.750
Yes!

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:47.830
All right!

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:53.620
Inazuma Japan performs timely team plays, ending in a goal by Matsukaze!

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.850
The match is over!

00:19:57.850 --> 00:20:01.340
Inazuma Japan wins 3-2!

00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:04.310
Yes! We won!

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:05.680
We won!!

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:08.180
That can't be...

00:20:09.130 --> 00:20:11.870
But we came so far...

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:18.910
It appears there's no other way but to acknowledge this team's potential.

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:19.940
Yes.

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:29.820
Honey.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.170
A foolish waste of time.

00:20:32.170 --> 00:20:35.380
He must be stopped from this ball-playing as soon as possible.

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:39.880
But he did his best in his own style, wouldn't you agree?

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:46.220
Manabe-kun.

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:49.890
You found it. The answer key to victory.

00:20:51.380 --> 00:20:52.360
Yes...

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:54.850
Um... Minaho-kun...

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:57.600
Well...

00:20:57.970 --> 00:20:59.290
Thanks.

00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:02.640
Same here.

00:22:54.220 --> 00:22:58.070
As we head for the finals, we're faced with a huge trial!

00:22:58.070 --> 00:23:00.980
Assemble together, Raimon's rivals!

00:23:00.980 --> 00:23:03.960
Next, Fierce Attack! Resistance Japan!!

00:23:03.960 --> 00:23:06.180
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:19.350
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:22.280 --> 00:23:25.710
I'll find the answer to victory!

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:26.660
That's all!
